> "If you need to compile CUDA code (for example, `.cu` files), then instead use [torch.utils.cpp_extension.CUDAExtension](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp_extension.html#torch.utils.cpp_extension.CUDAExtension). Please see [extension-cpp](https://github.com/pytorch/extension-cpp) for an example for how this is set up."

> **❌ MISSING:** No full `CUDAExtension` setup.py with `.cu` file lists or `nvcc` flags is provided in the content.

**Fallback setup.py (no CPython agnosticism)** — for when the extension uses non-stable CPython APIs:

